{"timestamp":"2026-02-03T13:25:10.953Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Explaining possible websocket connection issues**\n\nAnalyzing websocket \"connecting\" status points to the WS server being down, port conflicts, stale sessions, or cached browser issues. I'll explain these causes concisely in Russian, include steps to verify the WS server is running and on the right port, and suggest checking browser console and endpoints like `/api/terminal-config`."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-02-03T13:25:10.953Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Clarifying port mismatch and config file issues**\n\nThe terminal stays \"connecting\" likely due to websocket port mismatches if Next runs on 3001 and ws defaults conflict, or if `/api/terminal-config` fails to return the correct port because of missing or stale config files. I'll explain how the terminal fetches the ws port from a temp file and suggest verifying `/api/terminal-config` output and running processes to ensure ports align."}}
