{"timestamp":"2026-02-03T13:25:40.517Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Analyzing long \"connecting\" state causes**\n\nThe connecting state likely persists because the terminal socket never fires an `onopen` event, possibly due to a stale or unreachable WebSocket endpoint after the backend process dies or mismatched ports from stale /tmp files. This explains the UI stuck on \"connecting\" without error feedback."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-02-03T13:25:40.517Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Identifying race condition blocking session init**\n\nThe \"connecting\" hang stems from a race where `initSession` checks `sessionsRef.current` before it updates with the new session, causing an early return and no retry. Scheduling a retry with `requestAnimationFrame` when the session isn't found should fix the stuck state."}}
