{"timestamp":"2026-02-03T13:42:27.008Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Updating CSS for CRM layout**\n\nPlanning CSS changes to implement a two-column CRM layout with a left sidebar and top tabs, adjusting grid columns accordingly. I'll ensure full-height containers with internal scrolling by setting `.crm-layout` and `.crm-sidebar` for proper overflow and scroll behavior while preventing page-level scrolling."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-02-03T13:42:27.008Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Designing detailed CRM layout CSS and scroll behavior**\n\nRefining grid and flex layouts for `.crm`, `.crm-layout`, `.crm-sidebar`, and `.crm-main` for a two-column CRM style with fixed header and internal scrolling. Decided to style `.crm-sidebar` like `.panel` purely via CSS to avoid markup changes, adjusting tabs, sidebar tree, and terminal panes for proper sizing, overflow, and user preferences on terminal list placement and hiding side blocks."}}
