{"timestamp":"2026-02-03T18:28:16.359Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Tracing client-side WS connection issues**\n\nThe server connection seems fine, so I'm investigating client-side reasons the WebSocket might not open or signal open events, focusing on potential React key mismatches, stale refs, double invocation effects, dynamic imports, and possible caching of a null terminal port causing connection failures."}}
{"timestamp":"2026-02-03T18:28:16.359Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_reasoning","text":"**Diagnosing WebSocket connection timing and container mounting**\n\nI’m focusing on whether the terminal container ref is unset during initial initSession calls, causing the WebSocket connection not to open and status to stay at connecting. The mounting timing combined with React render effects and layout changes could delay or prevent container assignment, blocking initSession progress. Adding a WS open timeout error display will expose the issue. Next, I’ll try reproducing and inspecting with Playwright to see if the connection is blocked or code errors appear."}}
